WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.188
Here's the idea the guide is built
on: a score is not a verdict.

2
00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:07.751
The report compares each setting
with Microsoft's guidance,

3
00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:10.388
and it reads configuration
on the day it runs.

4
00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:12.877
It can't tell you which
finding to fix first,

5
00:00:12.877 --> 00:00:15.937
what a skipped test means,
or when a finding is closed.

6
00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:18.516
Those decisions belong to named people,

7
00:00:18.516 --> 00:00:21.563
and the report is the
evidence they decide with,

8
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:26.876
as the Zero Trust and Assessment book argues
in its chapter, Evidence, Not Verdicts.

9
00:00:26.876 --> 00:00:31.060
So every run is scoped, authorized
and pinned to a tool version,

10
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.850
and its output stays inside the boundary.

11
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:38.675
Every result is recorded twice, the
tool's value and a normalized one.

12
00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:42.668
Every finding gets an owner, a route
to the page that remediates it,

13
00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:44.813
and a weighted place in the backlog.

14
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:47.700
Every run is compared
with the last and sealed.

15
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.314
A finding is ready for closure when
every applicable state has evidence and

16
00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:57.140
a reassessment shows a pass; the authorizing
official or the assessor decides.
